      "writtenOn": "2021-01-15T08:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It needs provide uid to do permission check via Context#checkPermission() but the problem is we can\u0027t get the native service uids from installed packages(such as mediaserver, audioserver) and oem can have more native services. Besides, the high level permission of those native services are defined in data/etc/platform.xml which can get the info from SystemConfig.\n\nIn the past, we were encountered the permission problem from native services which would block networking for the service(b/128944261, b/132217906), so we must know the high level permissions for those native service.\n\nBut SysetmConfig is the internal service for frameworks only which cannot use by Connectivty mainline module. Therefore, I create this API that can only get the native service uids who define the INTERNET/UPDATE_DEVICE_STATS permission in platform.xml.",
      "parentUuid": "ca47888b_c9eea3d4",
      "revId": "b0b86b43258ef2bd62ae6bed7935a10f3a6b29b9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
